WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:01.719
Nami betrayed Luffy.

00:00:01.719 --> 00:00:04.290
Sanji abandoned him and beat him up.

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:06.350
And Robin framed Luffy for assassination.

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:12.370
In all these circumstances, Luffy forgave
his crewmates because of his kind heart and

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:13.750
his faith in their relationships.

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:17.689
But can you imagine what another pirate would
have done in these situations.

00:00:17.689 --> 00:00:19.810
What would the main antagonist Blackbeard
have done?

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:21.920
Or the ruthless Captain Kid?

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:26.859
Well, what would have happened if instead
of being kind-hearted and loving, Luffy was

00:00:26.859 --> 00:00:29.199
power-hungry and evil?

00:00:29.199 --> 00:00:34.480
Starting with chapter one when Luffy is first
inspired to become a great pirate by Shanks.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:39.640
This part of the story remains mostly the
same, except for one key difference.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:42.000
Luffy is still captured by bandits.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.780
Shanks still rescues Luffy and loses his arm,
and the iconic straw hat still gets passed

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:47.780
down to Luffy.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:54.090
However, the small difference comes when Shanks
tells Luffy that cannot join his crew.

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:58.510
In the original, Shanks tells Luffy that he
is too young to join the crew.

00:00:58.510 --> 00:01:04.479
But for the purpose of this video, Shanks
is going to tell Luffy that he is NOT STRONG

00:01:04.479 --> 00:01:07.260
ENOUGH to join the Red Hair Pirates.

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:14.210
And this small change is going to make Luffy
believe that he can only become a great pirate

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:17.280
by becoming that most powerful.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:24.229
And while already somewhat believes this idea,
for this video Luffy is taking it to an extreme

00:01:24.229 --> 00:01:25.229
level.

00:01:25.229 --> 00:01:29.440
And he’ll also learn from Lucky Roux that
in this world you must kill or be killed.

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:36.180
And you won’t believe how this small change
is going to affect the battle at Marineford

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:38.080
later on.

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:43.330
For now, Shanks still leaves Dawn Island and
Luffy spends ten years training before setting

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:45.189
out to gather his pirate crew.

00:01:45.189 --> 00:01:48.850
And unlike the other What If videos we’ve
done on this channel such as What if Luffy

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:53.450
had the Admiral’s Devil Fruits or What if
Luffy Joined Shanks’ crew, we are going

00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:59.900
to spend significant time focused on the East
Blue because the dynamics of the Straw Hat

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:04.189
crew are going to massively change.

00:02:04.189 --> 00:02:09.670
So Luffy sets out, eager to gather a crew
and fight anyone in his path.

00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:11.690
He still loves to have fun and party.

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:13.790
He still wants to become the pirate king.

00:02:13.790 --> 00:02:17.910
And he still has a way of convincing people
to follow him.

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:23.050
However, now he is a power-hungry pirate.

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:27.180
He is more cold-hearted and he has less emotional
intelligence.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:33.970
Plus, he is willing to kill and he only wants
crewmates who are strong or useful to his

00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:34.970
crew.&nbsp;

00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:38.900
The first person Luffy meets is this pink
haired kid, Koby.

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:41.950
Luffy mocks the enslaved deck swab for being
such a weakling.

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:47.160
Luffy still clobbers Alvida and sets him free,
but instead of becoming Luffy’s friend,

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:52.310
this wanna-be marine now vows to one day take
down Luffy himself.

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:54.280
Next up is Shell Island.

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:58.920
Here Luffy would easily defeat the corrupt
marine captain Morgan and he would probably

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:01.739
laugh at seeing Zoro all tied up.

00:03:01.739 --> 00:03:06.560
Luffy would probably release Zoro after learning
that Zoro is a famous bounty hunter and then

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:08.050
challenges him to a duel.

00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:14.200
And even though swords are Luffy’s main
weakness, he would probably defeat Zoro because

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:17.819
the swordsman is weak from not eating for
so long.

00:03:17.819 --> 00:03:23.150
However, Luffy is impressed by Zoro’s strength
and instead of killing him, Luffy invites

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:24.450
Zoro to join his crew.

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:30.480
Which Zoro accepts because growing stronger
is also his main goal.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:35.730
The pair then travel to Orange Town, where
the story essentially plays out the same.

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:41.260
Luffy defeats Buggy and he lets Nami come
along because she is a badass navigator, something

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:43.330
the crew desperately needs.

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:47.159
And Nami would want to join because she can
steal Luffy's treasure later on.

00:03:47.159 --> 00:03:52.069
And speaking of treasure, this version of
Luffy would take most of the treasure from

00:03:52.069 --> 00:03:55.660
Buggy instead of leaving it for the ruined
town.

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:59.810
So even with the changes to Luffy, we still
have our first two crewmates.

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:05.290
And they would likely seek out other pirates
to fight and pillage before landing at Usopp’s

00:04:05.290 --> 00:04:07.079
hometown, Syrup Village.

00:04:07.079 --> 00:04:12.049
And this is where we have our first major
change to the story.

00:04:12.049 --> 00:04:17.859
After defeating the fake-butler Kuro, Luffy
never invites Usopp to join the crew because

00:04:17.859 --> 00:04:19.930
of his weak fighting capabilities.

00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:23.820
So sorry Usopp fans, our sniper stays at Syrup
Village.

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:26.800
But at least he gets the girl.

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:32.770
And no Usopp means no Merry, so Luffy and
the crew will need to steal a different ship

00:04:32.770 --> 00:04:35.080
somewhere along the way.

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:40.430
Next up is the Baratie, where the story takes
a dramatic&nbsp; turn for the worse.

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:45.990
The crew would still defeat this guy no problem,
but things get really interesting when the

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:49.740
world’s strongest swordsman Mihawk shows
up.

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:55.160
Because a battle-hungry Luffy would never
let Zoro have all the fun fighting such a

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:56.940
strong opponent.

00:04:56.940 --> 00:05:02.700
And there are a lot of ways that this battle
could go, but none of them are good for the

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:03.700
Straw Hats.

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:10.070
We already saw Zoro almost die from this encounter
and it could be even worse for Luffy because

00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:12.050
of his weakness to blades.

00:05:12.050 --> 00:05:16.780
It is likely he could lose an arm or leg in
this fight, but let’s just assume that he

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:25.380
gets a similar massive injury like Zoro which
means that the crew must stay at the Baratie

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:26.380
while they heal.

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:31.420
And during this time, Luffy convinces Sanji
to pursue his dreams of finding the All Blue,

00:05:31.420 --> 00:05:34.790
so the cook joins the crew as well.

00:05:34.790 --> 00:05:40.319
But this prolonged recovery leaves Nami with
the perfect chance to betray Luffy.

00:05:40.319 --> 00:05:44.600
She steals the treasure, and the ship, and
returns to her home island where she hopes

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:47.180
to pay for her village’s freedom.

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:54.610
This leaves Luffy pissed off by not only his
defeat to Mihawk, but that his crewmate would

00:05:54.610 --> 00:05:56.720
betray him.

00:05:56.720 --> 00:06:02.509
So we head to Arlong Park, where an enraged
Luffy storms in, defeats the fishman Arlong

00:06:02.509 --> 00:06:05.100
who is terrorizing Nami’s village.

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:07.910
And Luffy is furious that Nami betrayed him.

00:06:07.910 --> 00:06:13.050
He could even threaten to destroy her village
himself, but let’s assume that he eventually

00:06:13.050 --> 00:06:20.009
allows her to rejoin because he respects what
she was doing to protect her people and her

00:06:20.009 --> 00:06:21.520
use to the crew.

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:24.360
Certainly, that takes a different kind of
strength.

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:30.000
But now Nami and Luffy’s relationship is
much shallower than it was in the original

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.000
story.

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:36.569
So while Luffy is still saving islands from
other bad pirates, he is not gaining as many

00:06:36.569 --> 00:06:41.500
friends and allies because he is fighting
for selfish reasons.

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:46.820
Keep watching to see how this will become
a fatal flaw later on.

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:52.090
At this point, we’ve got the whole crew
minus Usopp as they reach Logue Town, the

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:54.650
last island before the Grand Line.

00:06:54.650 --> 00:07:00.280
Here Luffy is never captured by Buggy because
well, Buggy is no longer alive.

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:01.280
Yikes…

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:06.560
But Luffy is still helpless to fight the marine
captain Smoker, who ate the Smoke logia devil

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:07.560
fruit.

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:12.699
Luffy is still saved by his father dragon,
but the defeat leaves Luffy desperate to learn

00:07:12.699 --> 00:07:14.919
how to fight Logia devil fruit users.

00:07:14.919 --> 00:07:21.099
So instead of a party as the crew enters the
Grand Line, an angry Luffy is just determined

00:07:21.099 --> 00:07:22.259
to get stronger.

00:07:22.259 --> 00:07:27.540
Now the first person they meet in the Grand
Line is the former pirate king’s doctor,

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:28.540
Crocus.

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:33.720
And being a former Roger pirate means that
he would surely know the basics of haki.

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:39.360
So with the defeat to Smoker still on his
mind, Luffy convinces Crocus to teach him

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:42.160
how to defeat Logia fruit users.

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:47.009
This would require some time, but eventually
the crew would learn the basics of Armament

00:07:47.009 --> 00:07:49.020
and Observation haki.

00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:53.509
And damn that’s going to make a huge difference
to every single fight ahead.

00:07:53.509 --> 00:08:00.009
Vivi, the princess of Alabasta, might still
tag along with the hope that Luffy could save

00:08:00.009 --> 00:08:01.009
her kingdom.

00:08:01.009 --> 00:08:05.289
She could even tempt Luffy with the promise
of a strong opponent to fight on her home

00:08:05.289 --> 00:08:06.289
island.

00:08:06.289 --> 00:08:11.180
However, when the crew arrives on Drum Island,
I don’t think they could convince Chopper

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:16.539
to join them because Luffy would care more
about his monstrous powers instead of his

00:08:16.539 --> 00:08:18.300
capabilities as a doctor.

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:25.610
So no Chopper, but they do recruit some random
doctor to join their crew.

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:32.190
Next they travel to Alabasta, where Luffy
is itching to fight another warlord of the

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:34.740
sea after his defeat by Mihawk.

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:40.380
And now that Luffy knows the basics of Haki,
his fight with Crocodile goes much smoother.

00:08:40.380 --> 00:08:45.640
He can actually punch the Sand logia fruit
user and eventually manages to defeat him.

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:50.630
So with Crocodile down, we now reach another
interesting crossroads.

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:57.030
While I think Robin would definitely join
the crew, she would probably consider the

00:08:57.030 --> 00:09:01.839
straw hats to just be another group of bad
guys that she would stay with to progress

00:09:01.839 --> 00:09:02.940
her own plans.

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:07.780
But the more interesting questions would be
what happens with Crocodile?

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:13.720
You see, we have many examples of other strong
pirates recruiting defeated pirates to their

00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:14.720
crew.

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:18.480
For example, the Emperor of the Sea, Kadio,
tried to recruit Luffy after defeating the

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:20.920
straw hat captain in Wano.

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:26.430
So while it is possible Crocodile could be
arrested by the marines, this version of Luffy

00:09:26.430 --> 00:09:33.029
invites him to join the crew because he is
a powerful fighter.

00:09:33.029 --> 00:09:39.250
So with two new crewmates from Alabasta, we
continue to Jaya, and the fateful meeting

00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:42.710
with the darkness logia fruit user Blackbeard.

00:09:42.710 --> 00:09:47.500
After Luffy makes an example out of this springy
pirate he would certainly challenge Blackbeard

00:09:47.500 --> 00:09:48.870
to a fight.

00:09:48.870 --> 00:09:54.740
Blackbeard would welcome this because he is
already trying to capture Luffy to turn him

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:55.870
into the World Government.

00:09:55.870 --> 00:10:01.890
And with Luffy’s warped personality, these
two have actually become very similar.

00:10:01.890 --> 00:10:03.630
They are both hungry for power.

00:10:03.630 --> 00:10:08.540
They both believe in their dreams and are
willing to do whatever it takes to achieve

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:09.540
them.

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:12.220
And most importantly, they are both subscribed
to this channel.

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:17.279
But would you believe me if I told you that
this similarity will lead them to joining

00:10:17.279 --> 00:10:19.170
forces later on?

00:10:19.170 --> 00:10:21.190
Keep watching to find out why.

00:10:21.190 --> 00:10:27.100
But for now, we will assume that their fight
essentially ends in a draw, and the straw

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:29.550
hats fly up to the sky islands.

00:10:29.550 --> 00:10:33.430
Here they defeat the lightning fruit user
Enel much easier because of Luffy’s rubber

00:10:33.430 --> 00:10:37.550
body but also because of their experience
with haki.

00:10:37.550 --> 00:10:43.590
Luffy could even try to recruit Enel, but
I imagine Enel would probably decline.

00:10:43.590 --> 00:10:52.420
And at this point, Luffy’s bounty is significantly
higher than it was during the original story.

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:58.190
Luffy’s obsession with strength would likely
mean he doesn’t worry about causing destruction.

00:10:58.190 --> 00:11:04.089
So similarly to his rival Eustass kid, his
bounty would rise even higher.

00:11:04.089 --> 00:11:10.500
Next the straw hats face one of their toughest
challenges yet, the admiral Aokiji.

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:16.500
The chilly fruit user has come to reclaim
Robin, and he is simply too much for the crew

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:17.500
to take on.

00:11:17.500 --> 00:11:19.580
And this leads to an interesting dilemma.

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:24.290
Since this version of Luffy has much less
of a bond with his crewmates, it is possible

00:11:24.290 --> 00:11:26.480
he could abandon Robin.

00:11:26.480 --> 00:11:31.860
However, much like he welcomed Nami back,
in this case he surprisingly decides to challenge

00:11:31.860 --> 00:11:34.730
the admiral one on one for Robin’s freedom.

00:11:34.730 --> 00:11:40.800
And Luffy wouldn’t be as overwhelmed as
he was in chapter 321.

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:48.060
This version of Luffy is stronger and knows
haki, but he would still lose and have to

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:50.920
be saved by the crew’s doctor.

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:55.920
But this takes us to Water 7, where the crew
still needs a new ship after their crazy descent

00:11:55.920 --> 00:11:56.920
from Skypiea.

00:11:56.920 --> 00:11:59.730
This arc plays out similar to the original.

00:11:59.730 --> 00:12:03.610
Luffy already put his neck on the line for
Robin when he fought Aokiji, so he isn’t

00:12:03.610 --> 00:12:07.389
going to let the World Government take her
now.

00:12:07.389 --> 00:12:11.519
So the arc ends with Franky making them a
new ship before he joins the crew.

00:12:11.519 --> 00:12:16.950
And as an added bonus, Luffy is much more
interested in Franky’s weapons and he demands

00:12:16.950 --> 00:12:19.000
more guns on the new ship.

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:24.620
In their new ship, the straw hats seek out
fights with other strong pirates and marines

00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:30.270
in the Grand Line before eventually reaching
the zombie infested floating island, Thriller

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:31.270
Bark.

00:12:31.270 --> 00:12:34.630
Here Luffy stomps the warlord Gecko Moria,
and Brook joins the crew.

00:12:34.630 --> 00:12:40.440
And since the crew as a whole is much stronger,
they are also able to escape from the warlord

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:43.970
Kuma without much trouble.

00:12:43.970 --> 00:12:51.730
But next is Sabaody where the straw hats suffer
an EVEN WORSE defeat than they did in the

00:12:51.730 --> 00:12:53.120
original story.

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:58.600
In Chapter 506, we meet this old man, Silver
Rayleigh, who was the right hand of the former

00:12:58.600 --> 00:13:00.079
pirate king.

00:13:00.079 --> 00:13:05.300
And Rayleigh has actually been waiting for
Luffy since the time Shanks told him about

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:08.490
a certain kid who resembled their former captain,
Roger.

00:13:08.490 --> 00:13:12.630
And originally, Rayleigh helps the crew as
they prepare to enter the New World.

00:13:12.630 --> 00:13:16.830
But in this version, things are much different.

00:13:16.830 --> 00:13:21.360
Both Rayleigh and Shanks have heard of Luffy's
cold-hearted journey through the Grand Line

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:25.920
and they now believe that Luffy is not fit
to wear the straw hat.

00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:32.071
This leads Rayleigh to demand that Luffy change
his ways or give up the hat.

00:13:32.071 --> 00:13:39.000
Luffy, of course, wouldn’t pay him any attention,
which would lead to a mind-blowing confrontation.

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:42.760
Rayleigh challenges Luffy for the right to
the hat.

00:13:42.760 --> 00:13:44.630
And Luffy accepts.

00:13:44.630 --> 00:13:51.889
Of course, Rayleigh, who was said to be nearly
as strong as the former pirate king himself,

00:13:51.889 --> 00:13:56.420
would destroy Luffy and take the hat from
Luffy’s unconscious head.

00:13:56.420 --> 00:13:59.540
Bet you didn’t have that on your bingo card.

00:13:59.540 --> 00:14:02.860
This result could send the story in many different
ways.

00:14:02.860 --> 00:14:08.040
The first route we are going to explore has
Luffy staying on Sabaody where he vows to

00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:09.660
take the straw hat back from Rayleigh.

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:13.399
However, it is also at this time that the
World Government announces that Luffy’s

00:14:13.399 --> 00:14:15.430
brother, Ace, is going to be executed.

00:14:15.430 --> 00:14:17.830
So Luffy and the crew head to Marineford.

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:23.740
And just as much as Luffy wants to free Ace,
he is equally excited to fight all the crazy

00:14:23.740 --> 00:14:27.760
strong marines and pirates who are coming
to the war.

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:31.390
The straw hats arrive at Marineford just as
the battle is underway.

00:14:31.390 --> 00:14:35.401
And while this version of the straw hats are
definitely stronger than they were in the

00:14:35.401 --> 00:14:43.480
original story, they are still no match for
the combined might of Mihawk, the cyborg Pacifistas,

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:44.740
and the marine admirals.

00:14:44.740 --> 00:14:50.829
In this situation, it is also likely that
the Emperor of the Sea, Whitebeard, would

00:14:50.829 --> 00:14:52.050
not trust Luffy.

00:14:52.050 --> 00:14:56.509
So instead of being allies, they get in each
other’s way.

00:14:56.509 --> 00:15:02.570
This leads to Ace being executed as planned,
meaning Luffy failed even more miserably than

00:15:02.570 --> 00:15:04.459
in the original story.

00:15:04.459 --> 00:15:10.230
Perhaps a fitting lesson that the pursuit
of power will not always get you what you

00:15:10.230 --> 00:15:11.230
want.

00:15:11.230 --> 00:15:16.790
Assuming Luffy lives, he would likely be devastated
over the loss of his brother and humiliated

00:15:16.790 --> 00:15:18.640
that he was too weak to save him.

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:24.070
This could send him into an even deeper spiral
where he becomes more desperate for power.

00:15:24.070 --> 00:15:29.140
This mindset would set him on a similar track
to the last man that tried to take over the

00:15:29.140 --> 00:15:30.730
world, Rocks D. Xebec.

00:15:30.730 --> 00:15:35.900
While we don’t know much about this pirate,
we do know he was insanely powerful and tried

00:15:35.900 --> 00:15:37.300
to kill the world nobles.

00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:43.670
I think this Luffy would take the same path
AND meet the same end, where he would be killed

00:15:43.670 --> 00:15:46.769
in battle, never having regained his straw
hat.

00:15:46.769 --> 00:15:51.570
Now, let’s back all the way up to after
Luffy’s defeat to Rayleigh.

00:15:51.570 --> 00:15:58.670
From here, options two and three follow mostly
the same route.

00:15:58.670 --> 00:16:03.339
In the original story, Luffy punched this
world noble for trying to enslave his mermaid

00:16:03.339 --> 00:16:04.339
friend.

00:16:04.339 --> 00:16:09.649
While this version of Luffy wouldn’t necessarily
care about the slavery, I think his frustration

00:16:09.649 --> 00:16:14.880
after losing to Rayleigh could very easily
cause him to attack a world noble anyway.

00:16:14.880 --> 00:16:19.329
Just like in the main story, this would summon
the marines, the cyborg Pacifistas, and the

00:16:19.329 --> 00:16:22.050
admiral Kizaru to take out the straw hats.

00:16:22.050 --> 00:16:27.250
And while they might be able to survive the
Pacifistas and even Kuma, who they already

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:33.139
escaped from on Thriller Bark, in this version
Rayleigh would not save them from Kizaru.

00:16:33.139 --> 00:16:38.070
So Luffy would be captured, thrown in the
underwater prison, Impel Down, and erased

00:16:38.070 --> 00:16:39.160
from the story.

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:40.829
Or… not quite.

00:16:40.829 --> 00:16:46.060
Remember this is also around the time that
Blackbeard breaks into Impel Down to recruit

00:16:46.060 --> 00:16:48.120
strong criminals to his crew.

00:16:48.120 --> 00:16:53.830
So let’s assume that Ace is still taken
to Marineford, Blackbeard overthrows the prison,

00:16:53.830 --> 00:16:57.330
and he takes the strongest prisoners with
him.

00:16:57.330 --> 00:16:59.670
Including, are you ready…?

00:16:59.670 --> 00:17:00.670
Luffy.

00:17:00.670 --> 00:17:01.670
That’s right.

00:17:01.670 --> 00:17:06.079
Evil Luffy and Blackbeard are on the same
crew.

00:17:06.079 --> 00:17:07.079
For now.

00:17:07.079 --> 00:17:12.039
So, the Blackbeard pirates travel to Marineford
with the goal of killing Whitebeard and taking

00:17:12.039 --> 00:17:13.390
his devil fruit.

00:17:13.390 --> 00:17:20.329
However, this is where Luffy goes wild because
at this point Ace has already been executed.

00:17:20.329 --> 00:17:25.059
Luffy realizes that he failed to save his
brother because he was locked in jail.

00:17:25.059 --> 00:17:27.680
This causes him to lose his mind.

00:17:27.680 --> 00:17:30.420
He starts to fight anyone in his path.

00:17:30.420 --> 00:17:33.440
Admirals, Whitebeard’s commanders, Warlords
of the Sea.

00:17:33.440 --> 00:17:38.799
He would probably even awaken his conquerors
haki due to his immense rage.

00:17:38.799 --> 00:17:42.250
However, this is when Shanks shows up to stop
the war.

00:17:42.250 --> 00:17:45.000
Shanks demands that everyone stops fighting.

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:50.530
And while the Marines and other pirates pull
back, Luffy refuses to quit.

00:17:50.530 --> 00:17:56.120
Shanks is also wearing Luffy’s straw hat,
and, in a rush of madness, Luffy challenges

00:17:56.120 --> 00:17:58.750
Shanks to a duel for the hat.

00:17:58.750 --> 00:18:02.400
Now, consider how Shanks would be feeling
at this moment.

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:06.690
He is facing the kid who he once trusted with
his treasured straw hat.

00:18:06.690 --> 00:18:11.700
The kid who he hoped would grow up to become
the pirate king.

00:18:11.700 --> 00:18:18.770
But now standing before him is a twisted version
who has been driven mad by his lust for power.

00:18:18.770 --> 00:18:24.440
Shanks initially tries to talk Luffy out of
fighting, but Luffy will not give up and eventually

00:18:24.440 --> 00:18:30.590
Shanks agrees, hoping that he can teach Luffy
a lesson and get him to change his ways.

00:18:30.590 --> 00:18:39.230
But if they do fight, this version of Luffy
simply has no chance of defeating Shanks.

00:18:39.230 --> 00:18:45.440
And here is where we can split off into our
two final options for this Luffy's future.

00:18:45.440 --> 00:18:49.659
One way this could go is that Shanks takes
down Luffy, but as we’ve seen so often in

00:18:49.659 --> 00:18:52.900
the story, Luffy refuses to stay down.

00:18:52.900 --> 00:18:55.750
Even if Shanks begs him to stop, Luffy won’t
quit.

00:18:55.750 --> 00:19:00.760
He keeps coming for Shanks and the Red Hair
pirates, and ultimately Shanks is left with

00:19:00.760 --> 00:19:02.070
no choice.

00:19:02.070 --> 00:19:05.980
He kills the enraged Luffy.

00:19:05.980 --> 00:19:08.430
And you might ask why Shanks would kill Luffy.

00:19:08.430 --> 00:19:13.070
Well if Shanks thinks that Luffy would be
a danger to the world, similar to Rocks, then

00:19:13.070 --> 00:19:16.860
it would make sense for him to put Luffy down.

00:19:16.860 --> 00:19:26.080
And this takes us to a third path, and the
one we will explore more fully.

00:19:26.080 --> 00:19:31.549
Let’s imagine that Luffy has been knocked
down by Shanks again and again.

00:19:31.549 --> 00:19:38.059
Shanks’ blade rests on Luffy’s neck, and
finally, the rubber boy breaks down in tears.

00:19:38.059 --> 00:19:41.270
He lets all of his anger and his frustrations.

00:19:41.270 --> 00:19:45.950
He thinks back on his journey so far, and
all the cold-hearted things he’s done.

00:19:45.950 --> 00:19:49.850
And he finally realizes that he HAS lost his
way.

00:19:49.850 --> 00:19:54.420
After losing his brother in this battle, he
realizes that he cannot keep living like this.

00:19:54.420 --> 00:20:06.980
He wants to care about the people around him
and regrets not caring more about his crew.

00:20:06.980 --> 00:20:09.740
Seeing this, Shanks offers Luffy a choice.

00:20:09.740 --> 00:20:14.039
Come away from Marineford with him and to
learn how to be a great captain.

00:20:14.039 --> 00:20:15.710
Or die.

00:20:15.710 --> 00:20:21.000
Luffy accepts his former mentor’s offer
and after some time spent with the Red Hair

00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:23.980
pirates, he reunites with his crew.

00:20:23.980 --> 00:20:25.420
And this takes us to the time skip.

00:20:25.420 --> 00:20:29.919
But now instead of spending the two years
training separately, the crew spends the time

00:20:29.919 --> 00:20:35.240
bonding and forming the real relationships
that they had in the original story.

00:20:35.240 --> 00:20:40.360
After the time skip, the story would continue
much as it had in the original story, only

00:20:40.360 --> 00:20:44.919
with a few of the crew members missing.

00:20:44.919 --> 00:20:49.010
Luffy and crew advance through the New World
now with Luffy’s greatest power.

00:20:49.010 --> 00:20:53.960
His ability to inspire others with his joyfulness,
his friendship, and his selflessness.

00:20:53.960 --> 00:20:58.909
Which is a lesson he had to learn the hard
way because he tried to overcome everything

00:20:58.909 --> 00:21:02.260
with strength and power, but he failed.

00:21:02.260 --> 00:21:07.559
In the end he was not strong enough and he
nearly lost everything, including his brother

00:21:07.559 --> 00:21:08.559
at Marineford.

00:21:08.559 --> 00:21:12.310
But this leads to an even more interesting
question.

00:21:12.310 --> 00:21:16.910
What if Luffy was strong enough at Marineford?

00:21:16.910 --> 00:21:19.870
Could he have saved Ace if he had his current
storyline powers?

00:21:19.870 --> 00:21:24.520
In other words, what would happen if Gear
5 Luffy was at Marineford?

00:21:24.520 --> 00:21:29.390
If you want to find out, click this video
right here.

00:21:29.390 --> 00:21:30.179
Shanks for watching.

